Q4. Separate a rule from ML
Answer:

System A (Blocks form when empty): Exact rule

System B (Predicts needed practice questions based on past answers): ML

Q5. Separate ML from GenAI
Answer:

Tool predicting a film a viewer may like: ML

Tool writing a new two-line film description: GenAI

Hard
Q6. Compare two mechanisms
Answer:

Fixed login lock: Exact rule (or hardcoded logic)

Face check: Deep Learning (layered neural network)

Difference: The login lock relies entirely on fixed, programmer-written conditions that never change, whereas the face check automatically learns features from data, passing visual information through multiple stacked layers (from edges to shapes to full features) to recognize a face.

Q7. Correct two mixed-up claims
Answer:

Correction 1: Speed doesn't determine if something is ML; a simple calculator or hardcoded script responds instantly using fixed rules, not machine learning.

Correction 2: Deep Learning isn't just a vague term for "smarter AI"—it specifically refers to AI that uses multi-layered neural networks to learn complex patterns from data.

Example: An exact rule is a website form checking if an email field contains an "@" symbol.
